      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors \\(\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we can use the magnitude of the cross product of these two vectors. The magnitude of the cross product of two vectors in \\(\\mathbb{R}^3\\) gives the area of the parallelogram spanned by those vectors.\n\nThe cross product \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\) is given by the determinant of the followingmatrix:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{vmatrix}\n\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\\n3 & 1 & -2 \\\\\n1 & -3 & 4\n\\end{vmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThis determinant can be expanded as:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{i}(1 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot (-3)) - \\mathbf{j}(3 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot 1) + \\mathbf{k}(3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1)\n\\]\n\nSimplifying each component, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{i}(4 - 6) - \\mathbf{j}(12 + 2) + \\mathbf{k}(-9 - 1) = -2\\mathbf{i} - 14\\mathbf{j} - 10\\mathbf{k}\n\\]\n\nSo, the cross product \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\) is \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n\nThe magnitude of this vector is:\n\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-14)^2 + (-10)^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 196 + 100} = \\sqrt{300} = 10\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nThe area of the parallelogram is the magnitude of the cross product, so the area is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{10\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]",
