      "text": "To find the area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we need to calculate the magnitude of the cross product of these two vectors. The area \\(A\\) of the parallelogram is given by the formula:\n\n\\[ A = \\|\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\| \\]\n\nFirst, we compute the cross product \\(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\). The cross product of two vectors \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} u_1 \\\\ u_2 \\\\ u_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\\\ v_2 \\\\ v_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is given by the determinant of the following matrix:\n\n\\[ \\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ u_1 & u_2 & u_3 \\\\ v_1 & v_2 & v_3 \\end{vmatrix} = \\mathbf{i} \\left( u_2 v_3 - u_3 v_2 \\right) - \\mathbf{j} \\left( u_1 v_3 - u_3 v_1 \\right) + \\mathbf{k} \\left( u_1 v_2 - u_2 v_1 \\right) \\]\n\nSubstituting the components of \\(\\mathbf{u}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v}\\):\n\n\\[ \\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{i} \\left( 1 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot (-3) \\right) - \\mathbf{j} \\left( 3 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot 1 \\right) + \\mathbf{k} \\left( 3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1 \\right) \\]\n\\[ = \\mathbf{i} \\left( 4 - 6 \\right) - \\mathbf{j} \\left( 12 + 2 \\right) + \\mathbf{k} \\left( -9 - 1 \\right) \\]\n\\[ = \\mathbf{i} \\left( -2 \\right) - \\mathbf{j} \\left( 14 \\right) + \\mathbf{k} \\left( -10 \\right) \\]\n\\[ = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix} \\]\n\nNext, we find the magnitude of the cross product vector \\(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\):\n\n\\[ \\|\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-14)^2 + (-10)^2} \\]\n\\[ = \\sqrt{4 + 196 + 100} \\]\n\\[ = \\sqrt{300} \\]\n\\[ = 10\\sqrt{3} \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram is \\(\\boxed{10\\sqrt{3}}\\).",
